# Git & Commit Conventions

## Commit Message Format

### GitBook Auto-Exports (from GitBook UI)
```
GITBOOK-{change_request_number}: {change_request_subject}
```
Example: `GITBOOK-123: Fix documentation for settlement workflow`

### Manual Developer Commits
```
docs(<scope>): <short imperative description>

<optional body — what changed and why>
```

**Scopes:**
| Scope | When to use |
|-------|-------------|
| `article` | Creating or editing article content |
| `image` | Adding, replacing, or organizing screenshots |
| `config` | .gitbook.yaml, .cursor/rules, AGENTS.md changes |
| `taxonomy` | ARTICLE_TAXONOMY.md or Document-Format.txt changes |
| `nav` | SUMMARY.md navigation changes |
| `format` | Formatting, typo fixes, markdown cleanup |

**Examples:**
```
docs(article): add stablecoin settlement details to article 36
docs(image): capture issuer asset sale dashboard screenshot
docs(nav): add new Participation Agreements articles to SUMMARY.md
docs(config): update .gitbook.yaml redirects for renamed articles
docs(taxonomy): add articles 88-90 for Securitization module
```

## Branch Strategy

- `main` — production, synced to GitBook (protected)
- `refined3` — current working branch for major overhauls
- Feature branches: `docs/{topic}` for isolated changes

## Before Every Push

1. Verify no broken image references: `grep -r '!\[' *.md | grep -v 'images/'`
2. Verify SUMMARY.md matches article files
3. Verify all new images are in `images/{NN}-{kebab}/`
4. Run word count check: articles under 300 words need enrichment
